# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Environment Variables Example (.env.example)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Instructions:
# 1. Copy this file and rename it to `.env`:
#      cp .env.example .env
# 2. Add your Personal Access Token below (optional for local runs, but
#    recommended to avoid the 60 requests/hour unauthenticated rate limit
#    and to read private repo statistics).
#
# How to generate a GitHub Token:
#   GitHub Settings -> Developer Settings -> Personal access tokens -> Tokens (classic)
#   Scopes required:
#     - `repo` (if you want to include private repos/stats)
#     - `read:user` (to read profile stats)
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Your GitHub Personal Access Token (PAT)
GH_TOKEN=ghp_your_personal_access_token_here

# Alternatively, you can use GITHUB_TOKEN
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_your_personal_access_token_here
